.TH CSTRING_INSERT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_insert \- insert a C string at a given position
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_retval_t cstring_insert(cstr s, size_t pos, const char *str);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function inserts the null-terminated C string str at position pos of
s, and the characters at positions >= pos move right to make room. A pos
of 0 does the same as cstring_prepend(), and a pos equal to the length
does the same as cstring_append().
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s     String to change
pos   Insertion position (0 ... length, inclusive)
str   C string to insert (must not be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success              - The insert succeeded
ccol_invalid_args         - str is NULL, or pos > length
ccol_container_full       - The result would overflow a size_t
ccol_not_enough_memory    - The reallocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_append (3),
.BR cstring_prepend (3)
